course: dictionary
lesson: 11789
title: Belated: coming too late
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Belated means coming or happening later than it should have. If something is belated, it arrives after the time when it was expected. Context helps here, so look at the words around it.
explain: «Sorry for the belated birthday card, Sam!» The card came after the birthday, so it was late. Belated tells you the card should have come sooner.
explain: We often hear belated with wishes, thank-yous and apologies. «A belated thank-you» means you said thanks after you should have. The word tells you the lateness, and the thanks still count.
explain: Its adverb is belatedly, which tells you how something happened. «She belatedly remembered the library books» means she remembered late, a few days after she should have.
fact: Belated means coming or happening later than it should have.
fact: «Belated» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «a belated card» or «a belated thank-you».
fact: «Belatedly» is the adverb form, and it means late, or after the proper time.
fact: Check the meaning by swapping it in: «a late birthday card» means nearly the same as «a belated birthday card».
exercise: «Here is my belated birthday card, Sam!» What does belated mean? | Made of paper | Very early and bright | *Coming later than it should have | Lost forever
exercise: Mum says, «Sorry for my belated reply.» What does belated suggest? | *Her reply came late | Her reply was very long | Her reply was in a loud voice | Her reply was never sent
exercise: «Her belated card came a week after her birthday.» Find and copy the word that tells you the card was late. | birthday | week | card | *belated
test: «He gave a belated apology, two days after the argument.» What does belated mean here? | Said loudly in a crowd | Said before anyone asked for it | *Said later than it should have been | Said with a big smile
test: Which word is the adverb form of belated? | *belatedly | bell | belate | later
exam: «She belatedly said thank you for the gift.» What does belatedly mean? | Before the gift arrived | *Late, later than it should have been | Quickly and loudly | Happily, with a big smile
